 "_note": "Per-product header geometry at the two viewports AUDIT-10 measured as CORRECT, captured from the UNMODIFIED tree before PLAN-10 item 1's fix, with the document forced to Liberation Sans (the C49 control). plan10-header.js asserts the fix leaves every one of these within 2px. A global band is the wrong assertion here: the title column's width depends on how many action buttons the product has (btnCol is 244px without a PDF and 350.7px with one), so 'unchanged' has to be per product. NB these are LIBERATION-face numbers; the audit record's 431.4 / 557.4 were measured in the shipped DejaVu face on the same box.  RE-CAPTURED 2026-09-14 (Audit 9, A-9.P5a-6): the product header carried two names for one destination — the PDF control said \"Download PDF\" where the sticky bar said \"Data Sheet\", and the quote control said \"Request Quote\" where the sticky bar said \"Request a Quote\". Unifying them changes the button column width, so the pre-fix numbers cannot be kept as the reference. Every one of the 42 products moved by exactly one of TWO deltas at BOTH viewports — title +17.3 / btn -17.3 for a product with a PDF, title -10.0 / btn +10.0 for one without — which is the label change and nothing else; no product moved for any other reason and no overlap appeared. The PLAN-10 numbers this replaces are kept below under viewportsPrePlan10 so the original comparison is still readable.",
